WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:04.571
- Yo, what's up, guys? Nasher here coming to you from Seattle.

00:00:04.571 --> 00:00:07.440
As you may know, there's a new NHL team in town.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.709
And today we're showing you behind the scenes.

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:12.545
First things first, today it is bright and early here at 8:30 a.m.

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:14.347
The morning skate is getting ready to start up.

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:17.517
We're heading to the arena now, and we'll see what's going down.

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:19.486
We've just arrived here at Climate Pledge Arena.

00:00:19.486 --> 00:00:23.890
It is looking beautiful from the
outside and even better here on the inside.

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:25.992
Ever wonder what it looks like to be on an NHL bench?

00:00:25.992 --> 00:00:27.160
Well, we're out here chillin'.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:30.063
Nice little touch here in Seattle. For each of their warm-up pucks,

00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:33.133
we have the official warm-up puck: Seattle vs. New York.

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:35.869
So when you're taking home a puck from
the game, you know where it's from.

00:00:35.869 --> 00:00:38.471
So Climate Pledge Arena is all about the environment, right?

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:41.341
This is a fully electric Zamboni. Usually when we're down here,

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:43.877
you smell the gasoline. It sounds very loud.

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:48.148
As you can see, quiet Zamboni. Smells perfect. Beauty.

00:00:48.148 --> 00:00:50.417
And, of course, we have the Seattle Kraken locker room.

00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:52.519
Now, there's some top-secret stuff going on there right now.

00:00:52.519 --> 00:00:55.855
We're not able to enter, but let's walk down this tunnel behind you.

00:00:55.855 --> 00:00:58.525
You just feel powerful walking down a tunnel like this.

00:00:58.525 --> 00:01:01.728
Not only that, we have these crazy suites.

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:05.098
So Seattle had the optional skate before. The Rangers are in full force.

00:01:05.098 --> 00:01:08.768
- [Artemi Panarin:] The Rangers comin'.

00:01:08.768 --> 00:01:12.539
Not a lot of people have got to touch the
Seattle Kraken ice, and we are one of the few.

00:01:12.539 --> 00:01:15.075
All of this ice is from reused rainwater.

00:01:15.075 --> 00:01:18.645
They collect it. Bring it down here. Two Jumbos above us.

00:01:18.645 --> 00:01:20.180
You just cannot beat these vibes.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:20.647
Here we are

00:01:20.647 --> 00:01:23.249
We're joined with Philipp Grubauer here of the Seattle Kraken.

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:24.551
You've had a good couple of games here.

00:01:24.551 --> 00:01:25.318
You're starting tonight.

00:01:25.318 --> 00:01:25.785
How you feeling?

00:01:25.785 --> 00:01:26.619
- Pretty good.

00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:28.688
It's amazing to play in here for sure.

00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:30.090
- What's it been like in the locker room

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:31.758
kinda building a new culture here in Seattle?

00:01:31.758 --> 00:01:34.494
- It's been unbelievable to be part of that process

00:01:34.494 --> 00:01:37.230
and just to see the excitement in the city and

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:40.567
before we even started playing the first game here was incredible.

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:43.970
Playing a couple home games in a row, it's pretty cool and special,

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:48.007
and I think it translates to the excitement in the locker room for the guys as well.

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:49.943
- Tell me about the city of Seattle.

00:01:49.943 --> 00:01:52.212
What's something we should go check out after the game tonight?

00:01:52.212 --> 00:01:56.116
- Lake Union is incredible. Obviously go up the Space Needle.

00:01:56.116 --> 00:01:58.118
If you have time, there's so many great spots.

00:01:58.118 --> 00:02:01.888
You actually, you guys came in at the right time
because it's actually sunny today.

00:02:01.888 --> 00:02:03.790
- Yeah.
- For the last week, it's only been raining.

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:05.158
So just drive around the lake.

00:02:05.158 --> 00:02:08.061
I think that's pretty cool to see as
well. And Mount Rainier in the back,

00:02:08.061 --> 00:02:09.362
it's pretty special.

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:10.797
- Awesome, man. Wish you the best of luck tonight.

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:11.764
Thanks again for everything.

00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:12.832
And, uh, yeah.

00:02:12.832 --> 00:02:14.601
Phil Grubauer here with the Seattle Kraken.

00:02:14.601 --> 00:02:16.536
We explored the arena. We got on the ice.

00:02:16.536 --> 00:02:18.238
We got to talk to our boy Grubauer.

00:02:18.238 --> 00:02:20.440
What an unreal morning here in Seattle,

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:22.775
but now it is time to explore the rest of the city.

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:23.776
So we're going to go to the market.

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:24.944
We're going to grab some lunch.

00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:26.679
Show you guys around.

00:02:26.679 --> 00:02:28.848
We just saw the fish throw live in person.

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:31.818
This is where the Seattle Kraken announced their picks.

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:34.621
A fish came over, flipped it over. Bada bing!

00:02:40.527 --> 00:02:42.695
Dude, it is a whole different world here in Seattle.

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:46.299
We got the cats on the violin. I don't know what is happening, but

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:51.704
this place is sick. Markets, food, flying fish. You name it, they have it.

00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:54.607
We found a little card shop here at the market. The owner in there is super nice.

00:02:54.607 --> 00:02:58.211
We're going to walk in, show you guys around and maybe buy a couple packs.

00:02:58.211 --> 00:03:01.114
A lil' 1990 NHL Hockey cards.

00:03:01.114 --> 00:03:03.383
Dude, the Seals. Those jerseys are the best.

00:03:03.383 --> 00:03:05.385
All right, we've got our packs. We're gonna pop these open.

00:03:05.385 --> 00:03:08.855
We'll see if we can recognize any of the
players in here, depending on who we get.

00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:10.957
And a Mike Modano.

00:03:10.957 --> 00:03:13.393
That is a banger. North Stars jersey and all.

00:03:13.393 --> 00:03:14.961
Let's go grab some food. I'm starving.

00:03:14.961 --> 00:03:18.097
So we explored the market, found some food. We're at Athenian here.

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:21.100
Beautiful-looking food, seafood alfredo.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:23.603
We've got the fries. You can't beat the view.

00:03:23.603 --> 00:03:26.706
Out there we've got the Ferris wheel, which I think we're gonna head to next.

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:29.976
Yeah, I don't think I've been on a
Ferris wheel since I was seven years old.

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:33.279
This is fire. Man, Seattle literally has it all.

00:03:33.279 --> 00:03:35.982
We have made it to the top. Let's go! What a day.

00:03:35.982 --> 00:03:38.985
This is the perfect way to get ready for the Kraken versus the Rangers tonight.

00:03:38.985 --> 00:03:40.520
We've seen a lot of things here in Seattle.

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:42.021
We had to walk by the gum wall.

00:03:42.021 --> 00:03:44.757
I thought it was just a small little piece of a wall.

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:46.159
What is going on here?

00:03:48.127 --> 00:03:48.962
[Laughing]

00:03:48.962 --> 00:03:51.764
Best way to get around Seattle right now. We're gonna go right to the rink

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:53.666
on these little scoots. Let's get it.

00:03:56.869 --> 00:03:58.972
We are buzzin'! Let's go!

00:03:58.972 --> 00:04:01.708
In the arena, first stop, we gotta get decked out.

00:04:01.708 --> 00:04:03.376
Check out The Lair.

00:04:03.376 --> 00:04:07.013
No doubt, best merch, best branding in the NHL.

00:04:07.013 --> 00:04:09.682
Looking around, I mean—this, this is too much.

00:04:09.682 --> 00:04:12.452
There is a spinning, floating jersey rack.

00:04:12.452 --> 00:04:15.355
Rostislav Nasherov custom Kraken jersey coming soon?

00:04:15.888 --> 00:04:19.559
- [Announcer:] Your Seattle Kraken!

00:04:20.293 --> 00:04:21.527
- Let's go!

00:04:22.362 --> 00:04:24.063
We got the hookup here. We're gonna head to the media hole.

00:04:24.063 --> 00:04:25.865
They got us a little spot for warmies.

00:04:25.865 --> 00:04:28.635
Head down there, get a few of the boys. Let's go.

00:04:28.635 --> 00:04:31.471
We're gonna get you guys the best view ever of the warmies.

00:04:42.382 --> 00:04:51.691
- [Announcer:] Kraken Nation, It's time to release the Kraken!
- [Cheering]

00:04:55.395 --> 00:05:02.869
- And starting in goal, No. 31, Philipp Grubauer!
- [Fans:] Gruuuu!

00:05:12.278 --> 00:05:18.318
- [Fans:] Oooh.
- I mean, that's just a nasty snipe.

00:05:18.318 --> 00:05:22.588
Zero angle. Looked like it might've hit crossbar, but no, dead back of the net.

00:05:26.659 --> 00:05:30.363
What a start here in Seattle. A couple good chances both ways.

00:05:30.363 --> 00:05:34.067
1-0 for the Rangers right now. We've got a good view of the goal.

00:05:34.067 --> 00:05:35.368
We'll see what happens here in the second

00:05:36.436 --> 00:05:37.303
- Thank you so much.

00:05:38.438 --> 00:05:40.573
- Great to meet you. Enjoy the game.
- Yeah. You too.
- Appreciate it.

00:05:40.573 --> 00:05:42.809
Dude, Ohio represents out here.

00:05:45.445 --> 00:05:46.979
What up? How we doin' brother?

00:05:46.979 --> 00:05:48.481
- Good. How are you?
- Living the dream.

00:05:48.481 --> 00:05:50.183
- What is this? What is going on here?

00:05:50.183 --> 00:05:52.552
- So I made a sign that's spelled out in Russian.

00:05:52.552 --> 00:05:55.054
- That is sick. Dude, are you kidding me?

00:05:55.054 --> 00:05:57.123
- Jacob and Olly right here.
- Wow.

00:05:57.123 --> 00:05:58.624
- Rangers suck!

00:05:58.624 --> 00:06:00.193
- Thank you.
- Cool costume!

00:06:00.193 --> 00:06:03.062
- I think it's official. Olly and Jacob On the Bench, they're worldwide.

00:06:06.933 --> 00:06:11.437
- [Fan:] Yeah!
- [Cheering]
- [Foghorn blasting]

00:06:11.437 --> 00:06:13.806
- Big period there for the Kraken, tied the game up.

00:06:13.806 --> 00:06:15.341
Got to see it from multiple angles.

00:06:15.341 --> 00:06:18.044
I was up top. John was down low. Time for the biggies.

00:06:18.044 --> 00:06:19.779
We have the concessions coming in.

00:06:19.779 --> 00:06:23.149
The important thing to note about the concessions here, it is cashierless.

00:06:23.149 --> 00:06:26.285
There's cameras that follow you around the
store, and you don't have to do anything.

00:06:26.285 --> 00:06:28.955
You just walk in, insert your credit card and grab whatever you want

00:06:28.955 --> 00:06:30.857
off the shelves and then you're good to go.

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:34.260
Here we go.

00:06:34.427 --> 00:06:35.528
What are we feeling today?

00:06:35.862 --> 00:06:37.997
Don't mind if I do. How is it watching me right now?

00:06:37.997 --> 00:06:39.065
I have no idea.

00:06:39.532 --> 00:06:40.600
All right, water.

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:43.169
And just like that, no cashier needed. We're outta here.

00:06:45.471 --> 00:06:46.973
There, there's just no way.

00:06:46.973 --> 00:06:47.774
There's no way.

00:06:47.774 --> 00:06:49.142
Wow. The future is now.

00:06:49.142 --> 00:06:53.146
We got our Skittles. There's plants on the walls. There's no cashiers.

00:06:53.146 --> 00:06:54.080
This is a dream come true.

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:55.548
And a good hockey game to go along with it.

00:06:55.548 --> 00:06:57.350
We need a Seattle Kraken win.

00:06:57.350 --> 00:07:01.821
I'm not the curse, OK? I'm not showing up and getting them a loss. Let's go.

00:07:01.821 --> 00:07:04.624
Now we are going to the press lounge. We are going all over this building.

00:07:04.624 --> 00:07:07.293
The fans are to the left. The ice is to the right.

00:07:09.395 --> 00:07:10.463
Watch the game from here.

00:07:10.463 --> 00:07:13.366
That was actually nasty. Adam Fox with a little bop bop,

00:07:13.366 --> 00:07:16.002
double toe drag to the snipe. He is disgusting.

00:07:16.002 --> 00:07:17.537
We need a miracle. Let's go.

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:24.944
- [Fans yelling]

00:07:24.944 --> 00:07:27.046
How have they not scored one of these?

00:07:27.046 --> 00:07:32.819
Two goals, one minute. Pick up your phone, hold it.

00:07:34.053 --> 00:07:37.657
Final score, 3-1. RIP.

00:07:37.657 --> 00:07:41.561
And that is gonna do it here in Seattle. A tough loss to end the night.

00:07:41.561 --> 00:07:43.896
They just couldn't beat Igor. He popped off at the end.

00:07:43.896 --> 00:07:47.200
There were so many good chances, but it was too little, too late.

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:48.734
It was a blast here in Seattle, though.

00:07:48.734 --> 00:07:51.037
Getting to hang out with you guys, explore the arena

00:07:51.037 --> 00:07:54.307
and show you everything behind the scenes here at Climate Pledge.

00:07:54.307 --> 00:07:58.077
We'll definitely come back for another Seattle
game to prove that we are not the curse.

00:07:58.077 --> 00:08:00.046
So a crazy night, still a good night.

00:08:00.046 --> 00:08:02.882
Thank you guys for hanging out. I'm Nasher with B/R Open Ice,

00:08:02.882 --> 00:08:04.884
and we're out. Peace.

